# A stage0 sample from the audit: doubling a number until Int64 overflows,
# which traps (exit code 70) in the built executable as under `refined run`.
overflow is module
overflow purpose "Double a number until Int64 overflows, so the program traps"
overflow path overflow
overflow imports standard.console
overflow imports standard.math
overflow exports main

stdoutWriter is capability
stdoutWriter purpose "Authority to write lines to standard output"
stdoutWriter grants write console.stdout none

main is operation
main purpose "Print doublings until the multiplication overflows"
main invariant none
main typeParameter none
main input none
main output ExitCode
main outputOwnedBy none
main raises none
main effect write console.stdout
main uses stdoutWriter
main memoryHeap false
main async false
main maxRecursion none
main label begin loopKind none
main label begin within none
main label each loopKind while
main label each within none
main label each maxIterations limit
main label writeVDone loopKind none
main label writeVDone within each
main let v Int64 1 mutable
main let limit Int64 100 immutable
main let four Int64 4 immutable
main at begin goto each
main at each do double
main at each set v doubled
main at each do writeV
main at each branch ifError writeV goto writeVDone else goto writeVDone
main at writeVDone goto each

double is call
double in main
double invokes math.multiplyInt64
double argument left Int64 v copy
double argument right Int64 four copy
double result doubled Int64
double ownedBy none
double cleanedBy none
double borrows none
double catch none
double suppresses none

writeV is call
writeV rationale "The failure has nowhere to be reported, so it is discarded"
writeV in main
writeV invokes console.writeIntegerLine
writeV argument value Int64 v copy
writeV result none
writeV ownedBy none
writeV cleanedBy none
writeV borrows none
writeV catch writeVError console.WriteError
writeV suppresses console.WriteError.failed
